    "notes": "Six runs, selected by SUMER_FIXTURE_RUN (0-5); see the 'families' block for which triple of runs belongs to which cursor family. Every run's FIRST history.read carries no `page` field at all -- absent means 'from the start of available history' (spec/observation.md section 5, Ruling A8) -- and every page after it uses only a cursor the adapter itself returned; the suite never invents a cursor value. exact: the *_before run serves page 1 (e1,e2, next cursor h100) then EXITS instead of answering the h100 request -- the runner must kill/observe the crash, spawn *_after fresh, and resend cursor h100; *_after has no rule for anything except cursor h100/h200, so it will visibly fail (FIXTURE BUG stderr line, err.code=internal) if the runner resends anything else, which is the intended trip-wire for 'no event strictly before the resume cursor is re-emitted'. batch_restart: the *_before run serves the WHOLE first batch (f1,f2, next 'continue', batch NOT finished) then exits when asked to continue; because batch_restart only advances the durable cursor on next:null, the correct resume request is the ORIGINAL request -- an ABSENT page again -- and *_after's only rule matches that shape and re-serves f1+f2 before f3, exercising idempotent re-delivery (asserted by redelivered_on_resume) rather than the exact family's no-reemission guarantee. Each family declares the WHOLE sequence once, in expect.ledger, and its three runs read different amounts of it: the uninterrupted run emits all of it, the killed run a prefix, and the resumed run a suffix (exact) or the whole thing again (batch_restart). How much is owed is the RUNNER's call at four Truncated call sites in case_interrupted_pagination, never a key in here -- a fixture that could declare its own leniency would be the thing under test deciding how hard the test is. Truncated relaxes exactly one half, 'everything declared was emitted': wrong money inside the slice, a record nobody declared, and a non-contiguous slice (e1 then e3, the shape a re-emit-everything adapter cannot produce but a page-skipping one can) all still fail. Every entry names its AMOUNT, state, posting, surface and raw_sign, not just its local_id, for the same reason A5 compares the resumed live set's full financial content against the uninterrupted one: an adapter that returns exactly the right local_ids carrying entirely different money after a resume is precisely the failure this assertion exists to catch, and it is now caught twice -- once in the resumed run's own sequence, once in the folded bracket. expect.live is DECLARED per family, never folded out of expect.ledger, so a wrong fold is a difference instead of a coincidence."
